{"recordFormat":"standalone-source-scientific-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1.source-05","runId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1","caseId":"CURRENT-SOURCE-05","sourceGoalId":"hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-primary-active-ingredient-research-interplay-ab22c8c6","jurisdiction":"DE-HB","verdict":"accepted","verdictScope":"Only this exact current operative source row, with the complete mapped current target closure and explicit official qualifiers; machine candidate only","findingIds":[],"qualifierAndBroaderTargetBoundary":"HB theme4.3 common bullet5; theme compulsory in LK by official37. No universal GK duty inferred.","frozenScientificReasoning":"## CURRENT-SOURCE-05 — HB — ACCEPTED, bounded to theme 4.3 / LK\n\nSource key: `hb-chemistry-sekii-gyo2022-primary-active-ingredient-research-interplay-ab22c8c6`.\n\nOfficial page 36 common content bullet 5 requires describing the interplay of analysis, synthesis and Molecular Modelling in natural-/active-ingredient synthesis; page 37 supplies the LK theme qualification. `93a7ce4d-1c90-568c-9368-cac423011ef9` directly covers this interaction. Complete W1/W2 materials require assigning each method's contribution to the same research question, explaining feedback and responding to a model/experiment contradiction. Model fit is not accepted as an assay, 98% purity is not exclusive causal proof and a mixture's effect is not assigned to P. The more explicit explanatory treatment supports the source's descriptive duty without requiring learners to run a real synthesis or simulation. The current carrier is an HB LK target and absent from GK. This positive exact-row decision does not approve the remaining HB inventory.\n","rawFirstPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-source9-HB97-fresh-independent-b-v1/FIRST.independent-Source9-HB97.scientific.frozen.md","sha256":"b577d5418ad784c6c0f2fd2a7a26e1b90ffea34cfc935034f1f308e7e3d920d3","bytes":