{"recordFormat":"standalone-source-scientific-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1.source-06","runId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1","caseId":"CURRENT-SOURCE-06","sourceGoalId":"de-hh-chemie-sekii-bildungsplan-2022-3-1-072-b84cc8ad","jurisdiction":"DE-HH","verdict":"accepted","verdictScope":"Only this exact current operative source row, with the complete mapped current target closure and explicit official qualifiers; machine candidate only","findingIds":[],"qualifierAndBroaderTargetBoundary":"HH common basic/elevated nominal topic; assessment verb is explicitly derived from BNE context, not quoted as an original verb.","frozenScientificReasoning":"## CURRENT-SOURCE-06 — HH — ACCEPTED with literal/derived-operator distinction\n\nSource key: `de-hh-chemie-sekii-bildungsplan-2022-3-1-072-b84cc8ad`.\n\nOfficial page 31 contains the nominal item disposal/recycling of batteries and accumulators in the common section, before the additional elevated-level items. It does not literally contain the verb 'bewerten' in that item. The same page's BNE explanation supports a reasoned environmental teaching operationalization. The operative row explicitly distinguishes literal nominal source text from its derived assessment title/description; preserve this.\n\nWhole union: `c8844ac6-c414-5a0e-9fcd-7d0a82177d09` plus `f9e6d689-6e59-59a4-9f21-8c2d44413244`. c884 alone would focus too much on primary-cell operation and selection. f9e6 current P expressly treats both primary batteries and accumulators, uncontrolled release, controlled collection, actual recovery, energy/rest streams and a changed treatment/composition condition. This covers the nominal topic and the explicitly derived BNE discussion/assessment. It neither invents an official recycling-machine mechanism nor claims legal/safety authority or a universal environmental winner. The specific carrier is present in both HH course views.\n","rawFirstPin":{"