{"recordFormat":"standalone-source-scientific-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1.source-07","runId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1","caseId":"CURRENT-SOURCE-07","sourceGoalId":"mv-chem-sekii-mv-ch-sekii-2022-erprobung-q-galvanische-elemente-009-cf5ca0c7","jurisdiction":"DE-MV","verdict":"accepted","verdictScope":"Only this exact current operative source row, with the complete mapped current target closure and explicit official qualifiers; machine candidate only","findingIds":[],"qualifierAndBroaderTargetBoundary":"MV common unshaded GK/LK implementation/depth guidance; official rare-metals extraction/disposal/recycling sentence retained separately from editorial short source text.","frozenScientificReasoning":"## CURRENT-SOURCE-07 — MV — ACCEPTED with original rare-metals clause retained\n\nSource key: `mv-chem-sekii-mv-ch-sekii-2022-erprobung-q-galvanische-elemente-009-cf5ca0c7`.\n\nOfficial physical page 32 / printed 28 explicitly says to discuss disposal's environmental problems, extraction of **rare metals**, and recycling. It is unshaded common content in the right-hand Hinweise/Anregungen column beside secondary cells. Physical page 5 explains that this column supplies implementation guidance including necessary depth; it is not a literal new left-column bullet. The supplied short source text is an editorial compression; it must not erase 'rare metals' or masquerade as the exact official sentence.\n\nThe complete mapped union c8844ac6 + `f54b2c33-11f1-571f-aa1c-cf969cc141c4` + f9e6d689 now covers all three aspects. f54 explains an electrode-material need, ore grade, extraction conditions, water/residue consequences, co-product/boundary problems, argument/counterargument and a conditional conclusion. It distinguishes rare metals from rare-earth elements. f9e6 adds disposal/recycling for both source types; c884 supplies electrochemical-use context. Neither a generic battery comparison nor collection alone would have sufficed. Current specific carriers are targets in MV GK and LK. Detailed industrial extraction mechanisms and a quantified life-cycle assessment remain broader/absent requirements, not invented official duties.\n","rawFirstPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-source9-HB97-fresh-independent-b-v1/FIRST.independent-Source9-HB97.scientific.frozen.md","sha256":"b577d5418ad784c6c0f2fd2a7a26e1b90ffea34cfc935034f1f308e7e3d920d3","bytes":21541},"wholeOperativeSourceGoalDigest":"sha256:127b356b11e24c838d884e35b075e1239b17622e242cd6566d1f36676262d88e","wholePassagesDigest":"sha256:7715a6851e4ff1e2e52ac322a6cdf63be825157772e77f410eeb221a84a28912","currentMappingInputDigest":"sha256:27f11d0a2ef5c628fafaff554fad037c11aece7197908819892c99c1fa670966","wholeCaseInputDigest":"sha256:4dae74ccd0f406939fb77c9b28daa9b3c3b648bbed5224250ebcd66515a6735d","scienceProjectionPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-source9-HB97-whole-union-neutral-review-preparation-technical-v1/REVIEW.current-source9-whole-union-HB97.whole-scientific-inputs.no-old-verdicts.json","sha256":"dd7b8f863c4b1796d5abe37a25728c5e91bdea6d3c0cbc0e5e8764c610d42a48","bytes":2667378},"sourceExtractionPins":[{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-remediation14-guarded-root-integration-technical-v1/capsule/curricula/DE/Gymnasium/input/MV/upper-secondary/source-extraction/DE_MV_CHEMIE_SEKII_RAHMENPLAN_ERPROBUNGSFASSUNG_2022.source-extraction.json","sha256":"8a5de2a44c508207bc6ef462969aff6806d66e28e3ef92a5af68efa439a1d0bd","bytes":239721}],"currentMappingFilePins":[{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-remediation14-guarded-root-integration-technical-v1/capsule/curricula/DE/Gymnasium/mapping/DE-MV/upper-secondary/mv_chemistry_upper_secondary_source_extraction_to_canonical_chemistry.review.json","sha256":"6c9329cf8e03ae9367412a9597eac3fdca6217cda6977112c7f47f8e729e5684","bytes":264833}],"directMappedTargetIds":["c884