{"recordFormat":"standalone-source-scientific-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1.source-08","runId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1","caseId":"CURRENT-SOURCE-08","sourceGoalId":"de-nw-chemie-seki-klp-2019-Stufe1-4-metalle-und-metallgewinnung-bewertung-001-9298284d","jurisdiction":"DE-NW","verdict":"accepted","verdictScope":"Only this exact current operative source row, with the complete mapped current target closure and explicit official qualifiers; machine candidate only","findingIds":[],"qualifierAndBroaderTargetBoundary":"NW first-stage SekI. GK/LK are only technical CrossStage view packaging; own hypothetical decision is prospective, not observed household conduct.","frozenScientificReasoning":"## CURRENT-SOURCE-08 — NW — ACCEPTED, first-stage Sek I\n\nSource key: `de-nw-chemie-seki-klp-2019-Stufe1-4-metalle-und-metallgewinnung-bewertung-001-9298284d`.\n\nOfficial page 24 explicitly connects metal recycling, resource saving and energy saving to evaluating one's own consumption and disposal. The whole union is broad decision goal `1df17884-96ae-57d7-9da9-dbebd082596f` and specific `b7ae47da-6afa-5651-977a-3139af7d6eab`. The generic multi-criteria goal alone would not secure the metal/material and own-action duty. b7 explicitly joins both physical bases with a self-chosen hypothetical consumption/disposal decision. Its cases compare equal useful metal amounts, retained primary input, energy requirements and changed recycling conditions; consumption and return are both judged. The hypothetical choice is a valid prospective competence task, not a fabricated report of private household conduct or actual changed behavior. All five criteria/strategy-reflection duties of 1df are broader target obligations, not all demanded by this one NW sentence. GK/LK view inclusion is technical CrossStage packaging, not a Sek I course-profile requirement.\n","rawFirstPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20