{"recordFormat":"standalone-source-scientific-candidate-v1","recordId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1.source-09","runId":"chemie-current439-source9-HB97-independent-b-20261017-v1","caseId":"CURRENT-SOURCE-09","sourceGoalId":"sn-chem-seki-sn-ch-klassenstufe-8-lb5-035-01-d0f98a3c","jurisdiction":"DE-SN","verdict":"revise","verdictScope":"Only this exact current operative source row, with the complete mapped current target closure and explicit official qualifiers; machine candidate only","findingIds":["SB-S09a","SB-S09b"],"qualifierAndBroaderTargetBoundary":"SN grade8 LB5; binding left-cell introduction and indicator SE differ from recommended right-cell remarks; technical GK_LK is not an official grade8 course system.","frozenScientificReasoning":"## CURRENT-SOURCE-09 — SN — REVISE\n\nSource key: `sn-chem-seki-sn-ch-klassenstufe-8-lb5-035-01-d0f98a3c`.\n\nThe official grade-8 LB5 first row on physical 24 / printed 12 has the left-column introductory learning goal on everyday significance/use/handling, with classification, oxygen-containing inorganic acids, rules and acid rain in right-column remarks. Its indented **experimental examination of acidic solutions using indicators** is a left-column sub-duty, with SE in the remarks. Physical page 4 / printed IV states that learning goals/content are binding and remarks are recommendations. The current operative row concatenates these two columns into sourceText/rawSourceText and an ungrammatical derived description, without preserving the normative cells in this body. The passage's editorial-summary disclaimer is useful, but does not itself provide the missing per-fragment status in the goal body. 'GK_LK' here is technical metadata, not official grade-8 GK/LK courses.\n\nPositive whole-union coverage: current `e5d6de7e-28c5-5dd8-a700-ecc1a3a7b8cd` explicitly covers everyday significance, use and material-based handling; its cases distinguish constituent acid from aqueous mixture and do not turn natural origin or rough pH into a safety guarantee. `d2ccd1d5-56f7-583f-9724-e97441367f91` correctly requires using the particular indicator scale and only rough pH bands. Other mapped members (`1c1420c2`, `34da1a4c`, `580b3616`, `88ee181f`, `fd309753`) add conjugate pairs, advanced indicator electron models, gas detection, neutralization and ion-level interpretation. They are broader or adjacent content, not evidence that every duty of this row is met.\n\nFinding SB-S09a: preserve the left/right cell distinction, introductory depth and recommended status explicitly; do not upgrade acid-rain/classification remarks into independent universal mastery demands or claim advanced molecular indicator theory is required here.\n\nFinding SB-S09b: the mapped union has no current P demand for the learner actually to perform the acidic-solution indicator examination. Both d2 cases explicitly use teacher-provided observations/data; gas-identification P uses fictional demonstration protocols, and the other atoms are paper/model explanations. Reading colors and explaining mechanisms do not demonstrate the binding SE operator. The present source union is therefore incomplete even though its cognitive indicator/classification treatment is sound. A prospective supervised practical carrier with actual observed action/raw observations (or another source-faithful explicit allocation) is needed before complete source coverage can be accepted. This is a source/P performance-coverage finding; it does not assert that a real learner has failed, authorize a lab task, or reverse an unrelated D-description vote.\n","rawFirstPin":{"path":"/mnt/e/skillpilot-chemie-L7-20261017/current439-source9-HB97-fresh-independent-b-v1/FIRST.independent-Source9-HB97.scientific.frozen.md","sha256":"b577d5418ad784c6c0f2fd2a7a26e1b90ffea34cfc935034f1f308e7e3d920d3","bytes":21541},"wholeOperativeSourceGoalDigest":"sha256:62a09b277e2b642b8a974f4d46684ac843b7c9f2893a8983183a9289ea7e6895","wholePassagesDigest":"sha256